# Cloudflare Pages headers.
# Pages serves HTML at extensionless paths (/about, /research/), so a
# "/*.html" rule would never match a served page anyway.
#
# IMPORTANT: Cloudflare Pages MERGES Cache-Control from every rule that matches
# a path - it concatenates the values rather than letting the most specific
# rule win. An earlier "/assets/*  max-age=14400" rule therefore leaked into
# umbra.css and umbra.js (the live header became "max-age=14400, must-revalidate")
# and pinned the stylesheet to a 4h browser cache, hiding fresh deploys.
#
# Fix: keep exactly ONE Cache-Control rule so nothing can merge. Everything
# revalidates against its ETag, so a deploy shows up immediately and unchanged
# files (images, fonts) still come back as cheap 304s with no body transfer.
#
# The merge quirk is per-header, so the security headers below are safe to add
# here - just never introduce a second rule that sets any of the same names.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-ZQPejEVGAaxv6Ks7Vz7EG2WhGYp+N7AFqmkiLKZeYz8=' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Two policies, and a browser applies both:
# - The enforced one pins every source to this site plus the font CDNs and
#   Cloudflare Web Analytics (beacon script from static.cloudflareinsights.com,
#   reports to cloudflareinsights.com). It still allows inline script, because
#   the zone's JS-detections bootstrap is an inline script with a per-request
#   ray id: no hash can cover it and static Pages cannot add a nonce. Never add
#   a sha256 to this line: a hash makes browsers ignore 'unsafe-inline' and the
#   bootstrap would be blocked (build_indexes.py --check guards it).
# - The Report-Only one is the script-src lockdown on trial: browsers log what
#   it would block and block nothing. Its sha256 is the inline script in
#   404.html - edit that script and the hash must change too (--check fails and
#   prints the new one). Turn JS detections off in the zone before promoting it.
# Email Address Obfuscation injects /cdn-cgi/ scripts (same origin, allowed).
# A pages.dev preview never shows the zone's injected scripts (bootstrap,
# beacon), so check a policy change against the live HTML too.

# The pages.dev hostname serves the same site; keep it out of search results
# so only umbrasec.dev is indexed. Preview and branch aliases already get
# noindex from Pages. No other rule sets X-Robots-Tag, so nothing can merge.
https://umbrasec-dev.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Published tool sources are meant to be read and curl'd. Without these,
# .py/.kql/.md are served as application/octet-stream and .yml as text/yaml,
# and browsers download them instead of showing them - a bad look on a
# security site.
# Safe alongside the rule above: these set only Content-Type, and the merge
# quirk is per-header, so nothing collides with Cache-Control.
/tools/kev-watch/*
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

/tools/sigma-pack/queries/kql/*
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

/tools/sigma-pack/README.md
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

/tools/sigma-pack/rules/*
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
